<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-25 (native LOI/PSA Details, scope addition). Twin of
        LOI__c/fields/Selected_Offer__c - read that file for the full reasoning; everything it
        says about being a LINK rather than a copy, about being stamped onto the CHILD at insert
        (and therefore needing no Queueable), and about null being a normal non-error state
        applies here unchanged. THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY.
        ⚠ AMENDED 2026-08-25 AND UN-AMENDED 2026-08-26. The parenthesis above originally read
        "unlike Disposition__c.Primary_PSA__c". That lookup was deleted later the same day with
        the rest of the child-mirror family (manifest/remove-disposition-child-mirrors/) and
        RESTORED on 2026-08-26 when the user chose option A - keep the two lookups, rebuild the
        Details sections on SPANNING field items, leave the 15 formula mirrors deleted. So the
        original "unlike Primary_PSA__c" contrast is accurate again: that one writes back to the
        parent after the save and is deferred to DispositionPrimaryChildStampQueueable.
        THIS FIELD WAS UNAFFECTED BY BOTH SWINGS - it lives on Contract_Review__c and links to a
        real child record rather than mirroring one onto the parent.

        Stamped by DispositionStageEntryService.openDispositionContractReviews, in the same
        Database.insert that creates the Contract Review.

        ⚠ BLANK ON EVERY ACQUISITION CONTRACT REVIEW, PERMANENTLY, AND THAT IS CORRECT. This
        object is shared between the buy side (Opportunity__c populated) and the sell side
        (Disposition__c populated) - see the Disposition_PSA record type file for why a row must
        never carry both parents. Only the sell side has offers, so only the sell side ever
        carries a value here.

        deleteConstraint SetNull. relationshipName Selected_Offer_PSAs, distinct from the LOI__c
        twin's Selected_Offer_LOIs so the two child relationships on Disposition_Offer__c do not
        collide.

        FLS: read + edit on DPEG_Disposition_Edit (a lookup CAN carry editable = true; the
        human-editing half is the whole reason now), read-only on DPEG_Disposition_View.
        ⚠ The one-off backfill that was the other half belongs to the Disposition__c lookups, not
        to this field. It was retired on 2026-08-25 and came back on 2026-08-26 as
        scripts/backfill-disposition-primary-children.apex, whose DML is PLAIN (anonymous Apex
        cannot use SYSTEM_MODE) and therefore still needs the edit grant - on Primary_PSA__c, not
        here. Nothing backfills THIS field in any case.
    -->
    <fullName>Selected_Offer__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The selected Disposition Offer this PSA was raised against - stamped when the Contract Review is auto-created. Blank on acquisition Contract Reviews and on dispositions that never ran an offer round.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Opens the buyer offer this PSA came from. Set automatically when the Contract Review is created; blank if the disposition had no selected offer.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Selected Offer</label>
    <referenceTo>Disposition_Offer__c</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Contract Reviews (Selected Offer)</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Selected_Offer_PSAs</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
